  "id": "gdacs-exposure",
  "title": "GDACS Exposure",
  "description": "Population exposure records from the Global Disaster Alert and Coordination System (GDACS). Each record gives the modelled number of people inside the wind field of a tropical cyclone track point, for a stated wind threshold (39 kt or 74 kt). An exposure record counts presence in the hazard area. It does not count harm: the reported effects are in the `gdacs-impacts` collection. More information on the GDACS mapping in Monty can be found in the [GDACS Source Mappings](https://github.com/IFRCGo/monty-stac-extension/tree/main/docs/model/sources/GDACS#tropical-cyclone-advisory-timeline).",
